## Output — CSP Icons: Diagnosis & Fix Plan

### 1. Problem Summary
After a security hardening commit (`4a38874`), multiple FontAwesome 6 icons disappeared from the UI due to **Content-Security-Policy (CSP) blocking**. Affected icons include:

| Icon | Context |
|---|---|
| `fa-gamepad` | Sidebar next to MIST logo |
| `fa-bell` | Notification bell |
| `fa-xmark` | Close buttons (academic warning, modals) |
| `fa-triangle-exclamation` | Academic warning alert |
| `fa-wand-magic-sparkles` | Curadoria MIST section |
| `fa-chevron-left/right` | Game screenshot carousel |
| `fa-magnifying-glass` | Global search field |

### 2. Root Cause
The CSP header misplaces `https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com` under **`script-src`** instead of **`style-src`**, and omits it entirely from **`font-src`**. FontAwesome is loaded via `<link rel="stylesheet">` and serves `.woff2`/`.ttf` font files — both are blocked by the current policy.

Two CSP-violation console errors occur:
- `Refused to load the stylesheet ... because it violates "style-src"`
- `Refused to load the font ... because it violates "font-src"`

### 3. Recommended Fixes

#### File 1: `frontend/nginx.conf` (~ line 16)
**Change:** Move `https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com` into `style-src` and add it to `font-src`. Also include `'self' data:` in `font-src` for resilience.



